.TH elf_find_segment_offset 3 "ELF Library Functions" "QuickJS" "ELF Library Functions"

.SH NAME
elf_find_segment_offset \- Find the segment offset in an ELF file

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/elf.h>
.B void* elf_find_segment_offset(range map, uint64_t offs);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B elf_find_segment_offset function searches for the segment that contains the specified offset within an ELF file.

The function takes two parameters:
.I map
A range structure representing the memory mapping of the ELF file.
.I offs
The offset within the ELF file that you want to find the segment for.

The function returns a pointer to the segment that contains the specified offset. If no segment contains the offset, the function returns 0.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B elf_find_segment_offset function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/elf.h>

int main() {
  // Assume map is a valid range structure representing the memory mapping of an ELF file
  range map;
  // Populate map with the appropriate values

  uint64_t offset = 0x1000;
  void* segment = elf_find_segment_offset(map, offset);

  if (segment != 0) {
    printf("Segment containing offset 0x%llx found.\n", offset);
  } else {
    printf("No segment contains offset 0x%llx.\n", offset);
  }

  return 0;
}
.!
